; tds — a client of Microsoft SQL Server over its own protocol, the
; Tabular Data Stream (version 7.4): logging in with a user and a password,
; scripts, statements with parameters through sp_executesql, rows of what
; a schema of the ordinary types holds. The modules: what goes on the wire,
; the connection, a pool of connections per scheduler thread.
;
; A connection is a TcpStream like any other, so a statement parks its
; task on the runtime's evented I/O and the scheduler runs other requests
; meanwhile.
;
; NOT in it: encryption of the session (tds/Conn.scaly says what that
; means), Windows authentication, the old text and image types, floating
; point and money in a result, more than one result of a statement told
; apart.

package scaly 0.1.0

define tds
{
    module Wire
    module Conn
    module Pool
}
